<section
  id="case-semester-project-1-logotype"
  class="fullscreen-section case-study-section"
  data-title="Case Study: Gemenskapet Science Museum — Logo Design | Katja Turnsek"
  data-description="Graphic design case study for a curiosity-led museum identity balancing playful science symbols with clear, scalable typography."
  data-case="semester-project-1"
  aria-labelledby="case-semester-project-1-logotype-title"
>
  <div class="rows">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="case-study-header">
        <p class="case-eyebrow">Graphic Design</p>
        <h1 id="case-semester-project-1-logotype-title">Gemenskapet Science
          Museum</h1>
        <p class="case-subtitle">A curiosity-led museum identity balancing
          playful science references with clarity and credibility.</p>

        <dl class="case-summary" aria-label="Project summary">
          <div>
            <dt>Role</dt>
            <dd>Brand identity and logo design</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Scope</dt>
            <dd>Individual Semester Project 1</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Audience</dt>
            <dd>Older children and young teens</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Tools</dt>
            <dd>Adobe Illustrator</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Outcome</dt>
            <dd>Web and print logo suite</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>

        <div class="tech-demo-wrapper case-demo-wrapper">
          <div
            class="demo-links"
            data-auto="demo"
            data-case="semester-project-1-logotype"
          ></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <h2 class="case-section-heading">The brief</h2>
      <p>
        Gemenskapet Science Museum needed an identity that encouraged young
        visitors to explore while still feeling credible to families and
        schools. The mark had to communicate science and discovery quickly,
        remain legible across web and print, and adapt from a full bilingual
        lockup to a compact standalone icon.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <div class="case-study-grid">
        <article class="case-study-block case-study-block--challenge">
          <h2>Challenge</h2>
          <p>
            The identity needed to combine several fields of science without
            becoming visually crowded. It also had to balance a friendly,
            youthful tone with the trust expected from an educational museum.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Represent discovery without relying on a single science subject</li>
            <li>Keep multiple symbols clear when the mark is reduced</li>
            <li>Balance a playful icon and tagline with a grounded wordmark</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class="case-study-item case-study-media--explore">
          <img
            class="thumb"
            src="{{base}}assets/images/logosuite-gemenskapet-science-museum-900.webp"
            data-src="logosuite-gemenskapet-science-museum-900.webp"
            data-path="assets/images"
            width="900"
            height="638"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Gemenskapet Science Museum logo suite showing primary, secondary, icon, vertical, monochrome, and reversed versions"
          />
          <figcaption class="case-caption">Flexible logo suite for wide,
            compact, monochrome, and reversed applications</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <article class="case-study-block case-study-block--decisions">
          <h2>Key decisions</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Used a magnifying glass as the central metaphor for investigation,
              curiosity, and learning
            </li>
            <li>
              Divided the lens into coloured fields with molecule, atom, and
              network symbols to represent different scientific disciplines
            </li>
            <li>
              Paired rounded icon geometry with a clear sans-serif wordmark to
              keep the identity approachable but credible
            </li>
            <li>
              Added the handwritten Swedish tagline “utforska tillsammans :)” as
              a warmer layer that can be removed in smaller applications
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class="case-study-item case-study-media--booking">
          <img
            class="thumb"
            src="{{base}}assets/images/icon-gemenskapet-science-museum-600.webp"
            data-src="icon-gemenskapet-science-museum-600.webp"
            data-path="assets/images"
            width="600"
            height="435"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Standalone Gemenskapet Science Museum magnifying-glass icon with science symbols and Swedish tagline"
          />
          <figcaption class="case-caption">Standalone icon for compact and
            recognisable applications</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row case-outcome">
      <h2 class="case-section-heading">Outcome and reflection</h2>
      <p>
        The final system feels youthful without losing educational credibility.
        Its full lockups provide context for first-time visitors, while the
        standalone magnifying-glass symbol remains recognisable in compact
        placements. Creating one-colour and reversed variations alongside the
        primary version made scalability part of the design process rather than
        a later adjustment.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="back-to-work-container">
      <a
        href="{{base}}#work"
        class="label-link back-to-work-label"
        data-back
        data-back-fallback="{{base}}#work"
